#pragma once

// Files VaultLib saved, repaired as they load. VaultLib is heyitsleo's C#
// library (its source and Attribulator's are in quirk-analysis/); the community
// Attribulator and OGVI save with it, and it marks every bin it writes: StrE
// starts with "Generated by VaultBoy by heyitsleo". It writes every game's
// vaults its own way, and the games and other tools don't read all of it:
// NFS-VltEd throws on its chunk order in Most Wanted, Carbon and Pro Street,
// and OGVI's Carbon attributes.bin had a class too short for its fields, which
// Attribulina refused (crashdumps/crash5).
//
// Database calls these as each vault loads. What they correct gets a warning
// and marks the vault repaired (Vault::repaired): its pack loads dirty, so the
// next save writes it as the game's own files are. What can't be corrected is
// only warned about. What VaultLib writes, and what happens to it:
//   - World's final build's header on every vault, whatever the game (Vers
//     0x6838F8C1836A18DE, StrN before DepN, EndC chunks; VaultWriter.cs,
//     Chunks/VLTVersionChunk.cs): the target game's header again
//     (RepairHeader). Most Wanted's own vaults have no Vers chunk.
//   - A class's layout size from a running sum (ModernBase/Exports/ClassLoad.cs
//     ComputeBaseSize) that counts 8 bytes for every array header, where an
//     array of 16-aligned elements has 16, and an array's definition count for
//     its length, which some classes leave 0. A 16-aligned field after such an
//     array hides the first, a less aligned one doesn't: Carbon's visuallook
//     came out 1104 for 1112, Undercover's collisionsfx_core 52 for 132. A
//     class whose fields run past its size takes their end (RepairLayoutSize,
//     whoever wrote the file).
//   - mEncodedTypePad 1, 2 or 8 by the elements' alignment (VLTArrayType.cs),
//     where the games have 0, or 0x8000 for 16-byte elements: the games'
//     value (RepairValues). The game rewrites it as it loads.
//   - World's gpcore.bin with VaultData slot 0 (Attribulator's
//     VaultSlotExport.cs), where retail has -1 (every event vault 0): -1.
//   - The game's classes' collection reserves, layout sizes and counts, key
//     shifts and static sizes by rules of its own (ClassLoad.cs), and World's
//     gameplay static block left out: a class whose fields are as Attribulina's
//     list of the game's classes has them takes the list's values and bytes.
//   - Undercover's and World's index tables with no values block, mVals at
//     whatever follows (Static_Inorder_N_to_1.cs), and speech's the wrong way
//     round: a table that doesn't hold is written again from the class's
//     collections, which are all in its vault (Edit.h RebuildIndexTables). The
//     order of a parent's children is theirs, not retail's, which isn't kept.
//   - Undercover's vinyl layers with four bytes written 0 (VinylLayer.cs,
//     VinylColor.cs) and autosculpt aliases without their sliders (Alias.cs):
//     a warning, as the values aren't in the file. Lost without a warning, as
//     no retail value shows it: StringKey hashes worked out from the text
//     (a mangled name's original), entries for fields the class lacks (World's
//     coop_pursuit_1), values above 1 in bytes it reads as bools (Undercover's
//     ParticleAnimationInfo.RandomStartFrame, a paint's mMaterialFlags), and
//     edits of fields its types can't hold (DecalLayer, World's power-up
//     records).
//   - Bin strings nothing points at (VaultBoy's two), PtrN entries for null
//     pointers, 0x80 pack alignment, unaligned definition blocks: the writer
//     leaves them out or lays them out again, as it always does.
//   - mNumClasses, mDefaultDataSize, entries by field name, children in
//     reverse, Lua repacked as JDLZ (the same Lua unpacked): read and kept, as
//     the game reads them.
//   - World's event vaults saved by OGVI as VPAKs in the folder above
//     gc.vaults, without their VaultData export (Attribulator's own WorldProfile
//     saves them to gameplay\ in the event vault format): FolderPacks loads such
//     a file in place of the gc.vaults copy it has the name of, and
//     MoveToEventVaultFile makes it that event vault file again.
// VaultLib writes little-endian only (a plain BinaryWriter): PC files, and
// Carbon's PS2 ones through Attribulator's CarbonProfilePs2, whose 4-byte bools
// its 1-byte Bool can't write. Its files are read as any other.
// Pro Street's files aren't repaired past what every game's get (its camera
// lists and tiers VaultLib breaks, FEPartData.cs). Most Wanted's other
// differences (PtrN nulls, 0 in vlt pointer slots, Lua placement) the writer
// lays out again.

#include "Database.h"

#include <string>

namespace attrib::vaultlib
{

	// The vault's bin starts its StrE with VaultBoy's "Generated by" string.
	bool Marked(const RawVault& r);

	// Before the vault's exports are read: sets Vault::vaultLib (marked, or
	// VaultLib's header on another game's vault) and gives the vault its
	// game's header back.
	void RepairHeader(Vault& v, const Target& t);

	// A collection of `cls` whose layout fields end at `fieldsEnd`, past the
	// class's layout size: the class takes that size. `vault` holds the
	// collection; both it and the class's vault are marked repaired.
	void RepairLayoutSize(Vault& vault, ClassDef& cls, const std::string& className, const std::string& where, uint32_t fieldsEnd);

	// After the collections and classes of a Vault::vaultLib vault are read.
	void RepairValues(Vault& v, const Database& db);

	// A file whose vaults VaultLib wrote (Marked), read from disk; false when
	// it isn't a pack.
	bool MarkedPack(const std::string& path);

	// `pack`, loaded from OGVI's VPAK save of one of World's event vaults,
	// becomes the event vault file at `path` (gc.vaults\<name>.bin): that
	// format, a VaultData export with slot 0 (gpcore's -1, as in the game's
	// files), a warning, and dirty, so the next save writes it there.
	void MoveToEventVaultFile(LoadedPack& pack, const std::string& path);

} // namespace attrib::vaultlib
